Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||05-25-2001||12:08 AM||||Huck , these aren't cheap, Were talkin lots of money for this custom made stuff...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Like I care..haha ..I made it for people to enjoy... <P>Free.99 will do nicely.<P>The thing is that there not BACKLIT!!! I'm using 84 front light gauges for my conversion. I can complete it take pics and you can tell me what you think. I got mine printed off on high quality poster paper with a laser printer , all gauges cost $9 to print. Look Amazing. I put a Pontiac racing logo on the speedo (small nice , not tacky). My tach has a 7000rpm Redline in hopes that I actually will do an engine conversion within the next year , as well it has a Lotus V8 crest on it which looks really really good.<P>I did this for a friend on his old datsun 240 , He loves them and has had them in the car for 2 years with no problems with the paper it's printed on , no fading , anything and they light up nice at night.<P><BR>Let me know and I can post the gauges on the net somewhere<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||05-25-2001||12:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by starfighter007@msn.com:<BR><B>I am intrested in  new gauge faces for mmy car not real pticular about white or black faces but more intrested in a higher mph such as 220mph and 10grand tach face .yes i woul be very intrested in new gauge packege stick on or what ever thanks in advance</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>There is a site online somewhere that is selling 240mph speedo kits for Fieros. For the life of me I can't figure out why but it you want it... At the posted speed limit, your speedo is only like 1/4 of the way up...<P>Someone here may know the site, or if not I will find it and post it..<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||05-25-2001||04:02 AM||||I made mine backlit green. Man what a job that was. Still not happy with it though. as the green is hard to get to light up efectively. Am considering changing all the light bulbs in the dashboard with flourescent green lights to get the right effect.<P>As mentioned they are reasonably easily made if you have the right printer. I made mine in layers printed on adhesive clear lamination sheets and 1 layer printed on paper. Stick the 3 layers together and you have a backlit light setup. Part of the trick is to make your backlit printout bleed further out than the detail face. The detail face is for apperance. It is  the transparent layer that provides the lighting and colours. Well as well as painting the inside of the gauge panel with new fluro paint.||||reg||1
